Master Evaluator

Then evaluation/evaluator.py simply orchestrates all the individual evaluators.

from evaluation.flight import evaluate_flight_agent
from evaluation.hotel import evaluate_hotel_agent
from evaluation.weather import evaluate_weather_agent
from evaluation.budget import evaluate_budget_agent
from evaluation.itinerary import evaluate_itinerary_agent
from evaluation.supervisor import evaluate_supervisor
from evaluation.final_response import evaluate_final_response


def evaluate_graph(state):

    results = {}

    results["supervisor"] = evaluate_supervisor(
        state["user_query"],
        state["selected_agents"],
        state["trip_constraints"],
        state["supervisor_reasoning"],
    )

    if state.get("flight_results"):
        results["flight"] = evaluate_flight_agent(
            state["user_query"],
            state["trip_constraints"],
            state["flight_results"],
        )

    if state.get("hotel_results"):
        results["hotel"] = evaluate_hotel_agent(
            state["user_query"],
            state["hotel_results"],
        )

    if state.get("weather_results"):
        results["weather"] = evaluate_weather_agent(
            state["user_query"],
            state["weather_results"],
        )

    if state.get("budget_results"):
        results["budget"] = evaluate_budget_agent(
            state["user_query"],
            state["budget_results"],
        )

    if state.get("itinerary"):
        results["itinerary"] = evaluate_itinerary_agent(
            state["user_query"],
            state["itinerary"],
        )

    if state.get("final_response"):
        results["final"] = evaluate_final_response(
            state["user_query"],
            state["final_response"],
        )

    return results
Why this design is better

This architecture follows the Single Responsibility Principle:

Each evaluator is responsible for one agent only.
Each file has its own prompt tailored to that agent's output.
You can improve or replace one evaluator without affecting the others.
If you later add a Visa Agent, Restaurant Agent, or Activities Agent, you simply create a new evaluator file and register it in evaluator.py.

This modular design is much closer to how evaluation pipelines are organized in production AI systems than putting all evaluation logic into one function.